content.text:
The spec reviewer found four real implementation ambiguities, all worth fixing before anyone codes:

- uninstall could otherwise leave Entire running through Lefthook;
- “unhealthy” did not distinguish currently broken from currently working-but-fragile;
- dead-owner sessions needed an explicit inclusion rule;
- hook-manager coexistence needed deterministic precedence.

I’m tightening those contracts now, then I’ll rerun the spec review before sending the implementation plan to its own reviewer.

