content.text:
The Task 2 quality review found a genuine security boundary and several correctness gaps:

- repository symlinks could redirect generated writes outside the worktree;
- `post-rewrite` stdin was not requested in the Lefthook config;
- health did not validate effective source-directory behavior;
- filesystem inspection errors and duplicate YAML keys could be misclassified;
- config publication could expose a partial installation.

These are valid for this codebase, especially because its existing `worktreedir`/`osroot` APIs are specifically designed to pin writes against symlink traversal. I’m sending all blocking findings back now; the transaction work will be pulled forward only as far as needed to make the artifact installer safe before Task 3 composes it with native-hook migration.

